<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21086" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hydaspes</span></b> , is,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑδάσπης</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river of India</i>, <i>a tributary
				of the Indus</i>, now <i>Jeloum</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 7,
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 20, 23, § 71</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 4, 5,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 12,
			8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 4, 211</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				22, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 8, 227 al.</span></i>—To denote
				<i>the East</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">repressor Hydaspis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 123 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hydaspēus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Hydaspes</i>, <i>Hydaspean;</i>
			<b>poet.</b> also for <i>Indian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemmae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. III. Cons. Hon. 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Erythrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 2, 447</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A companion of Æneas</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
				10, 747</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>An Indian</i> or <i>Ethiopian
			slave</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2, 8, 14</span></i>.</div>
